From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <iio-sensor-proxy@jayd.ml>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:04:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] main: Return pending Claim() calls when the last client
 releases

Claim() returns only after the sensor's first reading, so that the
client has a valid value right away. If the last client releases the
sensor (or leaves the bus) before that reading, polling stops and the
pending Claim() calls are never returned: the caller waits for its D-Bus
timeout, or gets NoReply when the daemon exits. KWin claims the
accelerometer only while the screen is on, and got NoReply this way when
the screen turned off just after iio-sensor-proxy had restarted.

Return them when polling stops for want of clients. This also sends a
driver change that was held back for a hotplugged sensor's first
reading; with no clients left there is nothing to wait for.
---
 src/iio-sensor-proxy.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
index bfc7ae8..6e2e16f 100644
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -429,6 +429,9 @@ client_release (SensorData            *data,
 	    g_hash_table_size (ht) == 0) {
 		SensorDevice *sensor_device = DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(driver_type);
 		driver_set_polling (sensor_device, FALSE);
+		/* The last client left before the first reading: no reading
+		 * will come to return the pending Claim() calls. */
+		maybe_notify_sensor_startup_finished (data, driver_type);
 	}
 }
 
